BOOT - choose the file a disk boots››Syntax:› BOOT [d:][path]file[.ext]››Marks a file on an EOSFS disk as the›program loaded by the boot sectors.›The file may be in any directory.››FORMAT writes the EOSFS loader. BOOT›records the file's first extent list›in sector 1. Erasing or replacing the›file clears the mark. The stock OS›cannot boot 512 byte sectors.››Example:› boot /dos/dos.sys››See also: COLD, FORMAT›